diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..51b8ba8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,25 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## On-device article translation
+
+Open **Translate articles** below the navigation, choose a language, and select
+**Translate**. The control translates the current page’s article headlines,
+summaries, captions, and body text, including related teasers. **Show original**
+restores the English text and can cancel an in-progress translation. Each language
+is translated from the original English rather than a previous machine translation.
+
+Translation uses the browser’s built-in `Translator` API on a supported device
+and secure origin (HTTPS or localhost). The browser may need a network connection
+to download language packs; article text is processed locally with no cloud
+translation fallback. Unsupported browsers or language pairs display a message
+and keep the original text available. Language availability depends on the browser
+and device. Choices apply to the current page; navigation does not trigger downloads.
+
+The implementation marks editorial text with `data-article-text` and changes text
+nodes only, preserving links and formatting. It leaves code blocks, advertisements,
+and interactive controls alone and releases translation resources on navigation.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
